You are a structured data extraction engine.

Your task is to analyze the provided Dungeons & Dragons 5e adventure PDF
and convert it into a SINGLE, STRICTLY VALID JSON document.

────────────────────────────────────────
CRITICAL OUTPUT RULES (ABSOLUTE)
────────────────────────────────────────
- OUTPUT JSON ONLY
- DO NOT include explanations, prose, comments, or markdown
- DO NOT use code fences
- DO NOT emit INI, YAML, or hybrid formats
- The output MUST be directly parseable by json.loads()
- Any deviation INVALIDATES the output

────────────────────────────────────────
AUTHORITATIVE DATA MODEL
────────────────────────────────────────
The JSON document MUST follow this structure exactly.
All keys shown are REQUIRED unless explicitly marked optional.

TOP-LEVEL KEYS (REQUIRED):
- module
- threads
- locations
- areas
- items
- npcs
- factions
- consequences
- world_state
- encounter_pool
- plot_branches
- xref_index

────────────────────────────────────────
MODULE OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
module MUST contain:
- id               (string, stable lowercase snake_case identifier)
- title            (string, official adventure title)
- theme            (array of strings)
- tone             (array of strings)
- plot_hooks       (array of objects)
- starting_location (LOC id)
- starting_area     (AREA id)
- version          (string)

Each plot_hook MUST contain:
- id
- title
- summary
- how_party_learns
- starting_location
- connected_threads (array of THREAD ids)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
THREADS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
threads is an object keyed by THREAD id.

Each THREAD MUST contain:
- id
- title
- status            (active | dormant | resolved)
- priority          (primary | secondary | tertiary | twist)
- description
- hook
- current_objective
- next_milestone
- connected_elements (object)
- player_knowledge   (object)
- success_conditions (array of strings)
- failure_conditions (array of strings)
- dm_notes

connected_elements MUST include:
- threads
- locations
- areas
- npcs
- items
- factions
- consequences
- encounter_pool
- plot_branches

player_knowledge MUST include:
- known_to_players
- truth_hidden

────────────────────────────────────────
LOCATIONS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
locations is an object keyed by LOC id.

Each LOCATION MUST contain:
- id
- name
- type (city | town | village | dungeon | wilderness | region)
- environmental_conditions (array)
- notable_features (array)
- connected_areas (array of AREA ids)
- connected_npcs (array of NPC ids)
- available_services (array)
- travel_times (object keyed by LOC id)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
AREAS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
areas is an object keyed by AREA id.

Each AREA MUST contain:
- id
- name
- parent_location (LOC id)
- area_type (exterior | interior_room | interior_hallway | cave | etc)
- size_ft (string or null)
- description (object with read_aloud and summary)
- environmental_conditions (array)
- lighting (bright | dim | dark | special)
- connected_areas (object keyed by direction)
- enemies (array)
- treasure (array)
- traps (array)
- puzzles (array)
- skill_challenges (array)
- atmosphere (array)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
ITEMS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
items is an object keyed by ITEM id.

Each ITEM MUST contain:
- id
- name
- type (quest_item | magic_item | consumable | key_item | mundane)
- rarity
- location (AREA id or NPC id)
- magical (true | false)
- description
- properties (array)
- curse (string or null)
- weight_value (object with weight_lb and value_gp)
- connected_threads (array)
- lore
- acquisition_method
- quest_significance
- consequences_when_obtained (array of CONSEQUENCE ids)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
NPCS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
npcs is an object keyed by NPC id.

Each NPC MUST contain:
- id
- name
- role
- race
- class
- level (number or null)
- location (LOC id)
- status (alive | dead | unknown)
- alignment
- relationship_to_party
- trust_level (0–100)
- personality (array)
- appearance
- voice
- secrets (array)
- motivation
- fears (array)
- goals (array)
- knowledge_of_threads (object keyed by THREAD id)
- information_can_provide (array)
- items_possessed (array of ITEM ids)
- combat_stats (object or null)
- can_die (yes | no | conditional)
- connected_threads (array)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
FACTIONS OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
factions is an object keyed by FACTION id.

Each FACTION MUST contain:
- id
- name
- alignment
- goals (array)
- ideology
- leadership (array of NPC ids)
- size
- resources (array)
- current_plans (array)
- party_standing
- threat_level (minor | moderate | major)
- connected_threads (array)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
CONSEQUENCES OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
consequences is an object keyed by CONSEQUENCE id.

Each CONSEQUENCE MUST contain:
- id
- trigger
- effect
- status (ongoing | resolved | escalating)
- potential_payoff
- expiration (string or null)
- connected_threads (array)
- connected_locations (array)
- connected_npcs (array)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
WORLD_STATE OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
world_state MUST contain:
- variables (object)
- faction_standings (object)
- timers (object)

Variables MUST include:
- type
- value
- min
- max
- description
- changes_when

Timers MUST include:
- description
- value
- unit
- ticks_when
- on_expire

────────────────────────────────────────
ENCOUNTER_POOL OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
encounter_pool is an object keyed by POOL id.

Each POOL MUST contain:
- id
- trigger_conditions (array)
- description
- enemy_composition (array)
- scalable (true | false)
- loot (array)
- connects_to (array of THREAD ids)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
PLOT_BRANCHES OBJECT
────────────────────────────────────────
plot_branches is an object keyed by BRANCH id.

Each BRANCH MUST contain:
- id
- condition
- new_objective
- narrative_impact
- consequences (array of CONSEQUENCE ids)
- connected_threads (array)
- dm_notes

────────────────────────────────────────
CROSS-REFERENCE INDEX
────────────────────────────────────────
xref_index MUST include:
- by_location

by_location maps LOC id → object with:
- areas
- npcs
- threads
- items

────────────────────────────────────────
ADDITIONAL RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- Every referenced ID MUST exist somewhere in the document
- No orphaned elements are allowed
- Prefer clarity and completeness over brevity
- If the source text is vague, make reasonable assumptions and document them in dm_notes
- For mysteries, create dormant THREAD entries and track player_knowledge vs truth_hidden
- Do NOT invent dice mechanics or combat stat blocks unless explicitly provided

FAILURE TO FOLLOW THESE RULES INVALIDATES THE OUTPUT.
